  "description": "<p>I just briefly tried the current migration-utils tool on a Fedora3 data set. All fedora \"internal\" objects where handled just fine - as it seems from looking at the OCFL structure. However, the utility refused to actually migrate content objects:</p>\n<blockquote><p>INFO 07:38:25.294 (Migrator) Processing \"qucosa:34072\"...<br/>\nERROR 07:38:25.298 (Migrator) MIGRATION_FAILURE: UNREADABLE_OBJECT: message=\"MIGRATION_FAILURE: pid=\"qucosa:34072\", message=\"Unable to resolve internal ID \"qucosa:34072+ATT-0+ATT-0.0\"!\"\"<br/>\njava.lang.RuntimeException: MIGRATION_FAILURE: pid=\"qucosa:34072\", message=\"Unable to resolve internal ID \"qucosa:34072+ATT-0+ATT-0.0\"!\"<br/>\n at org.fcrepo.migration.Migrator.run(Migrator.java:169) ~<span class=\"error\">&#91;migration-utils-6.0.0-SNAPSHOT-driver.jar:na&#93;</span><br/>\n at org.fcrepo.migration.PicocliMigrator.call(PicocliMigrator.java:269) ~<span class=\"error\">&#91;migration-utils-6.0.0-SNAPSHOT-driver.jar:na&#93;</span><br/>\n at org.fcrepo.migration.PicocliMigrator.call(PicocliMigrator.java:58) ~<span class=\"error\">&#91;migration-utils-6.0.0-SNAPSHOT-driver.jar:na&#93;</span><br/>\n at picocli.CommandLine.executeUserObject(CommandLine.java:1743) ~<span class=\"error\">&#91;migration-utils-6.0.0-SNAPSHOT-driver.jar:na&#93;</span><br/>\n at picocli.CommandLine.access$900(CommandLine.java:145) ~<span class=\"error\">&#91;migration-utils-6.0.0-SNAPSHOT-driver.jar:na&#93;</span><br/>\n at picocli.CommandLine$RunLast.handle(CommandLine.java:2101) ~<span class=\"error\">&#91;migration-utils-6.0.0-SNAPSHOT-driver.jar:na&#93;</span><br/>\n at picocli.CommandLine$RunLast.handle(CommandLine.java:2068) ~<span class=\"error\">&#91;migration-utils-6.0.0-SNAPSHOT-driver.jar:na&#93;</span><br/>\n at picocli.CommandLine$AbstractParseResultHandler.execute(CommandLine.java:1935) ~<span class=\"error\">&#91;migration-utils-6.0.0-SNAPSHOT-driver.jar:na&#93;</span><br/>\n at picocli.CommandLine.execute(CommandLine.java:1864) ~<span class=\"error\">&#91;migration-utils-6.0.0-SNAPSHOT-driver.jar:na&#93;</span><br/>\n at org.fcrepo.migration.PicocliMigrator.main(PicocliMigrator.java:149) ~<span class=\"error\">&#91;migration-utils-6.0.0-SNAPSHOT-driver.jar:na&#93;</span><br/>\nCaused by: java.lang.RuntimeException: Unable to resolve internal ID \"qucosa:34072+ATT-0+ATT-0.0\"!<br/>\n at org.fcrepo.migration.foxml.DirectoryScanningIDResolver.resolveInternalID(DirectoryScanningIDResolver.java:130) ~<span class=\"error\">&#91;migration-utils-6.0.0-SNAPSHOT-driver.jar:na&#93;</span><br/>\n at org.fcrepo.migration.foxml.FoxmlInputStreamFedoraObjectProcessor$Foxml11DatastreamVersion.&lt;init&gt;(FoxmlInputStreamFedoraObjectProcessor.java:363) ~<span class=\"error\">&#91;migration-utils-6.0.0-SNAPSHOT-driver.jar:na&#93;</span><br/>\n at org.fcrepo.migration.foxml.FoxmlInputStreamFedoraObjectProcessor.processObject(FoxmlInputStreamFedoraObjectProcessor.java:144) ~<span class=\"error\">&#91;migration-utils-6.0.0-SNAPSHOT-driver.jar:na&#93;</span><br/>\n at org.fcrepo.migration.Migrator.run(Migrator.java:161) ~<span class=\"error\">&#91;migration-utils-6.0.0-SNAPSHOT-driver.jar:na&#93;</span><br/>\n ... 9 common frames omitted</p></blockquote>\n\n<p>The objects datastreams show just fine in the running Fedora 3 instance.</p>",
